1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,137
Right. I've now almost succeeded in finalising plans for our tour,

2
00:00:06,137 --> 00:00:11,330
so I'll bring you up to date with what I know.

3
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:17,360
As you know, we're flying first to Munich, on Monday the 4th.

4
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:24,135
The flight is at 11.30, so it's too early to have lunch at the airport.

5
00:00:24,135 --> 00:00:27,946
I suggest we meet there for coffee at 10,

6
00:00:27,946 --> 00:00:33,450
which should give us plenty of time for breakfast before we leave home.

7
00:00:33,450 --> 00:00:39,770
When we arrive in Munich, we'll be met at the airport by Claus Bauer.

8
00:00:39,770 --> 00:00:42,640
Claus works for a tour operator

9
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:47,110
and he'll look after us for the time we'll be in Germany.

10
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:52,419
He's already liaised with the managers of the theatre we're going to visit,

11
00:00:52,419 --> 00:01:02,220
and he's also arranged for an officer of the National Theatre in Munich to show us round the theatre one afternoon during our stay.

12
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:05,480
Now last time we discussed this trip

13
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:11,220
I didn't have the precise cost for hotel rooms, but now I have.

14
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:13,780
The normal rate at the hotel

15
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:19,491
where we're staying is 150 euros a night for a double room.

16
00:01:19,491 --> 00:01:23,403
I'd hoped to get that down to 120 euros,

17
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:29,140
but in fact I've been able to negotiate a rate of 110

18
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:32,260
That'll be reflected in the final payment

19
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:35,830
which you'll need to make by the end of this week.

20
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:39,420
On Tuesday, the day after our arrival

21
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:46,044
I had hoped we could sit in on a rehearsal at one of the theatres,

22
00:01:46,044 --> 00:01:49,759
but unfortunately that's proved very difficult to arrange,

23
00:01:49,759 --> 00:01:58,580
so instead we'll have a coach trip to one of the amazing castles in the mountains south of Munich.

24
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:05,250
On Tuesday evening, we'll all have dinner together in a restaurant near our hotel.

25
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:09,283
From talking to you all about your preferences,

26
00:02:09,283 --> 00:02:17,350
it was clear that a typical local restaurant would be too meat-oriented for some of you.

27
00:02:17,350 --> 00:02:20,500
Some of you suggested an Italian restaurant

28
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:24,973
but I must confess that I decided to book a Lebanese one,

29
00:02:24,973 --> 00:02:30,590
as we have plenty of opportunities to go to an Italian restaurant at home.

30
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:39,010
On Wednesday afternoon, the director of the play we're going to see that evening will talk to us at the theatre.

31
00:02:39,010 --> 00:02:43,000
She'll describe the whole process of producing a play

32
00:02:43,540 --> 00:02:45,110
including how she chose the actors,

33
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:49,720
and, as the play we're going to see is a modern one

34
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,430
how she worked with the playwright.

35
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:59,513
Right. Now I'd just like to make a few points about the plays we're going to see,

36
00:02:59,513 --> 00:03:04,930
partly because it might influence your choice of clothes to take with you!

37
00:03:04,930 --> 00:03:09,440
The play we're seeing on Wednesday evening is a modern one

38
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:11,756
and we're going to the premiere,

39
00:03:11,756 --> 00:03:14,360
so it'll be quite a dressy occasion

40
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:18,180
though of course you don't have to dress formally.

41
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:21,675
I gather it's rather a multimedia production,

42
00:03:21,675 --> 00:03:26,669
with amazing lighting effects and a soundtrack of electronic music,

43
00:03:26,669 --> 00:03:33,660
though unfortunately the playwright is ill and is unlikely to be able to attend.

44
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:38,433
On Thursday we're seeing a play that was first performed last year,

45
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:42,120
when it was commissioned to mark a hundred years

46
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,990
since the birth in the town of a well-known scientist.

47
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:52,070
We're going to see a revival of that production, which aroused a lot of interest.

48
00:03:52,070 --> 00:03:57,310
Friday's play will really make you think hard about what clothes to pack,

49
00:03:57,310 --> 00:04:00,938
as it'll be in the garden of a palace.

50
00:04:00,938 --> 00:04:04,880
It's a beautiful setting, but I'd better warn you

51
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:07,790
there won't be much protection from the wind.

52
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:14,440
On Saturday, we're going by coach to a theatre in another town, not far from Munich.

53
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:18,181
This will be the opening of a drama festival,

54
00:04:18,181 --> 00:04:24,000
and the mayor and all the other dignitaries of the town will be attending.

55
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:29,184
After the performance, the mayor is hosting a reception for all the audience,

56
00:04:29,184 --> 00:04:33,570
and there'll be a band playing traditional music of the region.

57
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:39,328
And after having a day off on Sunday, our final play is on Monday,

58
00:04:39,328 --> 00:04:42,960
and it's in the stunning setting of the old Town Hall

59
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,730
which dates back to the 14th century.

60
00:04:46,730 --> 00:04:52,330
The performance marks the fifty years that the lead actor has been on stage,

61
00:04:52,330 --> 00:04:54,340
and the play is the one

62
00:04:54,340 --> 00:04:59,130
where he made his first professional appearance, all those years ago.

63
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:04,170
And the day after that, we'll be flying back home.

64
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:08,860
Now have you got any questions before I...
